35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, I found some interesting things! It seems like one neighbor has been really stressed about the bins. Also, most people are too kind to turn away late bags, which might be part of the problem!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit sad to hear that someone has been feeling stressed, isn't it? I hope we can find a way to lift that burden. I've learned some things that might help us avoid new troubles.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The truck arrives quite early, between 7:40 and 8:15. This means the pavement must be cleared before many of us are even awake. Additionally, permanent installations require a lengthy four-month filing process and multiple signatures.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that the frontages are all different sizes! One is super narrow, and some have driveways. Also, we're spending 34,000 yen a year just because bags are left open! That's a lot of money!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, Rin. That sum is a burden we must address. I have also learned that a new shelter could cost around two hundred forty-eight thousand yen, though a ward subsidy may cover forty percent of that expense.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, 34,000 yen is a lot! But @Asuka, if a permanent shelter takes four months to approve, maybe we should look for something faster so our stressed neighbor feels better sooner? What do you think?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very thoughtful point, Kenji. We must be careful not to rush into a solution that might cause new worries. I wonder if a permanent structure might actually make things more difficult in the summer?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, speed is important, but a temporary fix often creates more work for the people managing it. If we choose a fast option, we must ensure it doesn't just add another chore to someone's morning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right! But we also have to think about the space. I found out some frontages are really narrow! If we just put a big box anywhere, it might block the whole sidewalk for one person!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to consider both the space and the time. We must ensure that our solution does not place an undue financial or physical burden on any single neighbor, regardless of their frontage.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I really want us to be friends again! If we pick something that's fair and doesn't take too long, maybe everyone will stop being grumpy. Do you think a subsidy would make a big shelter easier to agree on?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"A subsidy is a wonderful help, Kenji. However, I worry that a large shelter might trap the summer heat and smells, making the corner unpleasant for everyone to walk past. Perhaps a simpler, fresher approach is better?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, smells are a concern, but the real issue is the labor. If we opt for a ""simpler"" approach, who is responsible for the daily upkeep? We cannot let this become another unpaid job for one person.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! That's what I'm worried about! If we just ""keep it simple,"" the person whose house it's in front of will probably end up doing all the cleaning. That's not fair at all!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that fairness is not merely about the division of labor, but also the division of cost. We must ensure the financial weight is shared with compassion for each household's unique circumstances.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I think we're all starting to see the big picture! We need something that's fair, doesn't cost too much, and doesn't make anyone feel like they're doing all the work. Let's find a way to make everyone happy!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is so heartening to see us all thinking of one another. Let us keep these worries in mind as we look at our options, so we can choose a path that brings true peace to our corner.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must be cautious. If the options we are about to see rely on ""voluntary"" rotations or ""informal"" agreements, they will likely fail or exhaust someone. I will be voting for the most structurally sustainable option.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm with Asuka! We need a real rule, not just a ""please help"" promise. If the bins stay in one spot, the person living there shouldn't be the only one cleaning up. Let's make it super fair!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"True fairness is a bridge built with both logic and empathy. As we move toward a decision, let us ensure our choice protects the peace of our hearts and the stability of our purses.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
