60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I'm worried about Option B! Moving the bins around might just start new fights between different neighbors. I think we should pick something that lets us all settle down and be friends again!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I understand your worry, Kenji. I also have concerns about Option A; a closed structure can trap such unpleasant smells in August. Perhaps Option C would be a gentler way to keep our corner fresh and tidy?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, Option C is the worst choice. ""Taking turns to oversee"" is exactly the kind of informal labor that falls on the most compliant person. It creates a recurring time burden without any structural solution.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I totally agree! Option C is just a fancy way of saying ""someone has to stand there and watch the trash."" That's not a solution, that's just a new chore!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"While Option C may seem gentle, it places a heavy burden on our time. Option B, though fair in theory, may cause unrest. Let us consider if Option A's cost can be shared with kindness.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I like that! If we all chip in for Option A, it's a permanent fix. It means no one has to move the bins or stand guard, so we can just be neighbors again!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"But dear Kenji, I worry that a permanent box might only hide the mess while making the smell worse for those walking by in the heat. Is there no way to keep it fresh?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, smells are a secondary issue compared to the labor of maintenance. Option A is the only one that removes the daily operational burden from the residents. It is a one-time effort for a permanent result.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait! Option A keeps the bins in the same spot! If they stay there, the person living right there still has to deal with it every day. Is that really fair, or just easier for everyone else?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your concern is valid. However, a permanent structure can be designed to be tidy and respectful. If we share the cost and the effort of the application, we create a lasting peace for all.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, maybe the structure makes it so much cleaner that the neighbor won't be stressed anymore? If we all help with the paperwork, it shows we care about them! I think Option A is the best for our friendship.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I appreciate your kindness, Kenji. However, I saw a bin house that could not be cleaned, and the smell was quite strong. I fear Option A might just trade one problem for another. Perhaps Option B is fairer?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, Option B is a logistical nightmare. Moving the point requires constant coordination and creates a new cycle of stress every time the location shifts. It doesn't eliminate the labor; it just redistributes the chaos.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right about the chaos! But @Kenji, just ""showing we care"" with paperwork doesn't change the fact that one person's front door is the trash zone forever. That's not fair! I can't vote for that!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"My dear Rin, fairness is a delicate balance. While the location is fixed, a shared investment in a proper structure elevates the point from a mere pile of waste to a community asset, easing the burden on that one home.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really want us to stop fighting! If we pick Option A and all work together to make it look nice and clean, maybe everyone will feel respected. I'm voting for Option A!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I wish for everyone's happiness, but I cannot ignore the smell of a hot August morning. I fear Option A will only bring new sorrows. For the sake of fairness and freshness, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is inefficient and Option C is an unsustainable labor trap. Despite the filing delay, Option A is the only choice that provides a structural solution and eliminates recurring chores. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I can't do A because it's not fair to the person living there, and B is too messy! But C is just a chore. I'll vote B because at least everyone shares the burden! I vote Option B!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"We must choose the path that offers the most enduring peace. While the cost is significant, the subsidy eases the weight, and a permanent structure removes the daily strife. For the harmony of our community, I vote Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
